message: "If you use or cite this demonstration, please cite it as below."
title: "The Sculptor and the Gardener"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jewell
    given-names: Jonathan D.A.
    alias: hyperpolymath
license: MPL-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/metadatastician/large-language-michelangelo"
url: "https://metadatastician.github.io/large-language-michelangelo/"
abstract: >-
  One form, two metaphysics: an interactive demonstration that
  generation-by-removal and generation-by-addition are the same act read in
  opposite directions. A deterministic voxel form is carved out of a solid
  block and grown from bare ground on one shared timeline, with live
  instruments reporting the actual render algebra rather than a scripted
  narration.
keywords:
  - generative-models
  - subtractive-generation
  - selection-from-prior
  - voxels
  - threejs
